  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-RosaNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"friendly\">\n      <prosody rate=\"96%\" pitch=\"+2%\">\n        Welcome to San Victor Island! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Today, <break time=\"300ms\"/> let&apos;s unlock analogies together. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Think of an <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"əˈnælədʒi\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">analogy</emphasis></phoneme> like a bamboo <emphasis level=\"moderate\">bridge</emphasis> between two word pairs. <break time=\"550ms\"/> When you see A <emphasis level=\"moderate\">is to</emphasis> B, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as C <emphasis level=\"moderate\">is to</emphasis> D, <break time=\"300ms\"/> here&apos;s how we say it out loud: A <emphasis level=\"moderate\">is to</emphasis> B, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as C <emphasis level=\"moderate\">is to</emphasis> D.\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
